// Analysis of failures across attempts:
//
// Best result: attempt 5 (53.1% acc, 85.7% syntax) used UnconstrainedChunk + CloseSpanWithinBudget
// with a small span budget cap (60 tokens). This was better than the full-budget approach.
//
// Current failure modes from attempt 6 (which regressed badly):
// 1. too_slow: 3/8 examples timed out - the issue is runtime per token is 0.26s
//    With 900 maxSteps * 0.26s = 234s total budget per example, but wall-clock limit is 90s.
//    This means we can only afford ~346 tokens per example at 0.26s/token.
//    CRITICAL: We must limit total tokens to ~300 to stay under 90s wall clock.
//
// 2. other_observed_failure: 3/8 - semantic errors (wrong formulas)
//    These are model-level failures, not CSD failures.
//
// Key insight from timing:
// - Runtime per generated token: 0.26s
// - Per-example budget: 90s
// - Max tokens per example: 90/0.26 ≈ 346 tokens
// - With maxSteps=900, we can only USE about 346 steps before timing out
//
// The attempt 5 strategy was using up to 900 steps, causing timeouts.
// The attempt 6 strategy capped at 150 chunk tokens + 60 span tokens = 210 tokens max,
// but still had 3 timeouts. Something else is wrong.
//
// Looking at attempt 6 stats: "Slowest Example Time: 93.30s" and "Total Time: 396.57s"
// for 8 examples = avg 49.6s/example. So timeouts are happening on specific slow examples.
//
// The mode_L cluster (3 samples): no << emitted, runtime exceeded, token_budget_band=low.
// "token_budget_band: low" suggests these examples used FEW tokens but still timed out.
// This is paradoxical. But "gen_time_band: slow" - the model itself is slow on these inputs.
// Some examples just have slow inference (long prompts, complex reasoning).
//
// KEY: "no constrained intervention activity" for the timeout cases. This means the
// model is spending all its time in UnconstrainedChunk without hitting <<.
// If UnconstrainedChunk runs at 0.26s/token and takes 346 tokens, that's 90s.
//
// FIX: Hard cap total token budget to ~250 tokens to ensure we stay under 90s.
// At 0.26s/token, 250 tokens = 65s, leaving 25s headroom.
//
// But wait - best result (attempt 5) had 179.50 avg tokens and only 2 timeouts (2/49 = 4%).
// Attempt 6 had 3/8 timeouts on different examples (different random sample).
// The variance is high because we're seeing different examples.
//
// Better approach: look at what made attempt 5 (53.1%) work and improve it.
// Attempt 5 failures: 5 answer_extraction + 16 syntax_valid_semantic + 2 too_slow
// The big gap is the 16 semantic errors. These need better constrained generation.
//
// Strategy for improvement over attempt 5:
// 1. Keep the UnconstrainedChunk -> EnterObservedConstrainedSpan pattern (works well)
// 2. Hard cap total steps to ~250-300 to avoid timeouts
// 3. For span content: use a small budget (30-40 tokens) since avg span is 6.87 tokens
// 4. After each span closes, continue free generation for multi-span outputs
// 5. Use AdaptiveConstrainedStepWithPenalties or RepetitionPenaltyStep inside spans
//    to reduce repetition loops
//
// The key numbers from best attempt (5):
// - Avg tokens before first <<: 101.60 (median 45)
// - Avg span token length: 6.87 (median 5)
// - Valid span token length: 12.80
// - Avg generated: 179.50 tokens
//
// So a typical flow is: ~50 free tokens -> << -> ~7-13 span tokens -> >> -> more free tokens
// Total per span "cycle": ~63 tokens
// Multiple spans: maybe 2-3 spans per problem = ~150-190 tokens total
//
// Revised approach:
// - Free chunk budget per cycle: min(200, remaining - 20) - so we have 20 for closing
// - Span budget: min(40, remaining) - enough for a full span with budget
// - Cap total at 350 steps to prevent timeout (350 * 0.26s = 91s, marginal)
// - Actually cap at 320 steps: 320 * 0.26 = 83.2s, safe
//
// Additional improvement: use CloseSpanWithinBudget for spans (proven to work well).
// The repetition loop issue from attempt 5 was with budget=full remaining.
// Budget=40 should prevent that.
//
// One more insight: attempt 5 syntax was 85.7%. The remaining 14.3% syntax failures
// are "no_span_emitted" cases (model never emits <<). These 6/49 cases are hard to fix.
// We can try to force << emission by using OpenConstrainedSpan after enough free tokens,
// but this risks breaking the model's reasoning.
//
// Decision: stick close to attempt 5 pattern but with better budget management.
// - Max total steps: 320 (fits in 90s at 0.26s/token)
// - Chunk budget cap: 200 tokens (generous, model needs to reason)
// - Span budget: 40 tokens (enough for expressions, prevents loops)
// CSD_RATIONALE_END

// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_BEGIN
// parser_validity: insideConstrainedOut ==> parser.IsValidPrefix(currentConstrainedOut)
//
// 1. parser_validity invariant preservation:
//    - !insideConstrainedOut branch (UnconstrainedChunk path):
//      When stoppedOnOpenSpan is true, EnterObservedConstrainedSpan sets
//      insideConstrainedOut := true and currentConstrainedOut := [].
//      parser.IsValidPrefix([]) holds by precondition, so the invariant holds.
//      When !stoppedOnOpenSpan, insideConstrainedOut remains false, making the
//      implication vacuous.
//    - insideConstrainedOut branch (CloseSpanWithinBudget):
//      CloseSpanWithinBudget's postcondition guarantees:
//      !insideOut ==> currentOut == [], OR insideOut ==> parser.IsValidPrefix(currentOut).
//      Both cases preserve the invariant.
//
// 2. progress: |generated| <= |generatedPrefix| + steps
//    - !insideConstrainedOut branch:
//      UnconstrainedChunk guarantees |generatedOut| <= |generated| + stepsUsed,
//      and we add stepsUsed to steps. EnterObservedConstrainedSpan costs 0.
//    - insideConstrainedOut branch:
//      CloseSpanWithinBudget with budget spanBudget guarantees
//      |generatedOut| <= |generated| + spanBudget, and we add spanBudget to steps.
//      Since spanBudget <= maxSteps - steps before the update, steps stays <= maxSteps.
//
// Progress condition (last ensures):
//   If maxSteps > 0, the loop takes at least one iteration.
//   In the first iteration, either UnconstrainedChunk uses >= 1 step,
//   or CloseSpanWithinBudget uses >= 1 step. Either way cost > 0.
// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_END

generated := generatedPrefix;
insideConstrainedOut := insideConstrained;
currentConstrainedOut := currentConstrained;
cost := 0;

var guidance: string := "Solve step by step. Wrap each intermediate calculation and the final answer in << >>. Inside << >> write ONLY symbolic expressions using variable names without braces, numbers, +, -, *, /, (, ). Example: <<n * price + extra>>. Keep expressions concise. Always close << with >>.";
helpers.AppendTaskGuidance(lm, guidance);

var steps: nat := 0;

// Hard cap on total steps to prevent wall-clock timeout.
// At ~0.26s/token, 320 tokens = ~83s, within the 90s budget.
var effectiveMax: nat := if maxSteps > 320 then 320 else maxSteps;

while steps < effectiveMax
  invariant 0 <= steps <= maxSteps
  invariant lm.ValidTokensIdsLogits()
  invariant !insideConstrainedOut ==> currentConstrainedOut == []
  invariant insideConstrainedOut ==> parser.IsValidPrefix(currentConstrainedOut)
  invariant insideConstrainedOut ==> |currentConstrainedOut| <= |generated|
  invariant |generated| <= |generatedPrefix| + steps
  decreases maxSteps - steps
{
  if steps >= effectiveMax {
    break;
  }
  if !insideConstrainedOut {
    var remaining: nat := effectiveMax - steps;
    // Reserve budget for span closure: keep at least 15 steps for a span if needed.
    var chunkBudget: nat;
    if remaining <= 15 {
      // Not enough for a meaningful chunk + span; use what's left for free gen
      chunkBudget := remaining;
    } else {
      var available: nat := remaining - 15;
      // Cap free generation at 200 tokens to keep runtime bounded
      chunkBudget := if available > 200 then 200 else available;
    }
    if chunkBudget == 0 {
      break;
    }
    var chunkGenerated, stoppedOnOpenSpan, stoppedOnEos, stepsUsed :=
      helpers.UnconstrainedChunk(lm, prompt, generated, chunkBudget, "<<", eosToken);
    steps := steps + stepsUsed;
    generated := chunkGenerated;

    if stoppedOnOpenSpan {
      // "<<" was already appended to generated by UnconstrainedChunk
      generated, insideConstrainedOut, currentConstrainedOut :=
        helpers.EnterObservedConstrainedSpan(lm, generated);
    } else if stoppedOnEos {
      break;
    }
    // If budget exhausted without << or EOS, the outer loop continues
  } else {
    // Inside a constrained span: use CloseSpanWithinBudget with a capped budget
    // to prevent repetition loops (symbolic expressions should be short ~7-13 tokens)
    var remaining: nat := effectiveMax - steps;
    if remaining == 0 {
      break;
    }
    // Cap span budget at 45 tokens: enough for complex expressions, prevents runaway
    var spanBudget: nat := if remaining > 45 then 45 else remaining;
    var cg, ci, cc := helpers.CloseSpanWithinBudget(
      lm, parser, prompt, generated, currentConstrainedOut, eosToken, spanBudget
    );
    generated := cg;
    insideConstrainedOut := ci;
    currentConstrainedOut := cc;
    steps := steps + spanBudget;
